# UADS V2 Cursor rules

UADS V2 is a NexLabs project and a controlled continuation of UADS V1.

## Source of truth

Before material work, read in this order:
1. `docs/v2/11-CHECKPOINT.md`
2. `docs/v2/10-DECISIONS-LEDGER.md`
3. `docs/v2/03-SCOPE.md`
4. `docs/v2/09-DEFINITION-OF-DONE.md`
5. `docs/v2/04-ARCHITECTURE.md`
6. `docs/v2/02-REQUIREMENTS.md`
7. `docs/v2/13-REVIEW-PROTOCOL.md`
8. active Work Order / Context Lock / Evidence Bundle.

Inherited V1 docs remain authoritative where the V2 overlay does not explicitly supersede them. Git/repository evidence prevails over conversational memory.

## Use the globally installed UADS

- Prefer the globally installed UADS V1 runtime/skill for engineering execution while UADS V2 is under construction.
- Start with `uads doctor` and `uads status` when host execution is available.
- Use `skills/uads-orchestrator/SKILL.md` and the global Cursor adapter contract.
- Runtime state stays under `~/.uads/`; do not create project-local caches, runtime work orders, indexes, model state or review archives.
- Repository `.engineering/` files are static governance/evidence only.
- Do not assume a V2 feature is available before its Work Order is APPROVED and merged.

## Temporary V2 construction guard

Until BUG-UADS2-001 is implemented and validated, do not manually fan out parallel review/specialist agents for this repository. Keep coordinator work plus at most one specialist active at a time when the host permits that control.

Until BUG-UADS2-004 is implemented and validated, do not claim automatic model/effort routing exists merely because it is planned.

## Governed delivery

- Use one stable Work Order identity across branch, PR, Context Lock, evidence, corrections and checkpoint delta.
- Freeze exact base/head identities.
- Implement only the active Work Order.
- No broad cleanup, dependency upgrade, migration, destructive action or product-scope expansion without explicit scope.
- If a critical canonical source changes, mark Context Lock STALE, re-inspect and relock.
- Run selected verification based on risk/impact and capture evidence.
- Review using HEDS-compatible delta-first progressive disclosure.
- Verdict is exactly APPROVED, CORRECTION REQUIRED or BLOCKED.
- CORRECTION REQUIRED stays in the same Work Order/PR when safe.
- Never advance with a known HIGH/CRITICAL defect.
- Checkpoint promotion occurs only after objective approval.

## Current bootstrap

Active bootstrap Work Order: `UADS2-BOOTSTRAP-001`.

Runtime V2 module implementation is not authorized until this bootstrap is APPROVED and merged.
